message.content:
Sure! Below is a simple example of an “interactive card” that rotates when you hover over it.  
It uses only **HTML** and **CSS** (no JavaScript).  

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* Basic reset */
body { margin: 0; padding: 0; font-family: Arial, sans-serif; background:#f0f0f0; display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; height:100vh; }

/* Card container – keeps perspective so rotation looks 3‑D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    perspective: 800px;          /* gives depth to the 3‑D transform */
}

/* The actual card – front & back sides */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth animation */
    transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3‑D space */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover triggers rotation */
.card:hover { transform: rotateY(180deg); }

/* Front side */
.front, .back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%; height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden;     /* hide backside while rotated */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 15px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
}

.front { background:#fff; display:flex; flex-direction:column; justify-content:center; align-items:center; }
.back  { background:#fafafa; transform:rotateY(180deg); display:flex; justify-content:center; align-items:center; }

/* Content styling */
h2 { margin:0; color:#333; }
p  { margin:5px 0 0; color:#666; font-size:.9em; text-align:center; max-width:80%; }

/* Optional: add a little image or icon */
img { width:60px; height:auto; margin-bottom:10px; }
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card">
    <!-- Front side -->
    <div class="front">
      <img src="https://via.placeholder.com/60" alt="Icon">
      <h2>Front Title</h2>
      <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Back side -->
    <div class="back">
      <h2>Back Title</h2>
      <p>Hover again to see more info or flip back.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

1. **Perspective** – The `.card-wrapper` sets `perspective: 800px;`.  
   This gives the 3‑D effect when the card rotates.

2. **Transform style** – The `.card` has `transform-style: preserve-3d;` so its child elements (`.front`, `.back`) stay in 3‑D space.

3. **Rotation** – On hover, the card is rotated 180° around the Y‑axis:  
   ```css
   .card:hover { transform: rotateY(180deg); }
   ```

4. **Backface visibility** – Both sides have `backface-visibility: hidden;` so the reverse side disappears when not visible.

Feel free to replace the placeholder image, change colors, or adjust dimensions to fit your design. Happy coding!
